            "review_title": "Review at Bề Bề Nội - Hương Vị Hà Nội Xưa",
            "review_text": "Mike\n5 contributions\n0\nThe Most Loaded and Flavorful Bún Riêu Bowl I’ve Ever Had!\nNov 2025 • Friends\nIf you’re looking for an unforgettable bowl of bún riêu, Bề Bề Nội is the place you shouldn’t miss. Despite the name, this is not a seafood restaurant—it’s a cozy spot specializing in bún riêu with some of the most generous toppings I’ve ever seen.\n\nThe bowl comes packed with a little bit of everything: bề bề (mantis shrimp), fish cake, lá lốt meat rolls, giò tai (pork ear sausage), peeled shrimp, crispy fried tofu, beef slices, pork cartilage ribs, and of course, fresh crab paste. Each component adds its own texture and flavor, creating a beautifully balanced and hearty bowl that feels both indulgent and comforting.\n\nThe broth is outstanding—clear, fragrant, and delicately sweet, with a natural richness that reveals how much care goes into preparing it. Every spoonful is satisfying, and the aroma alone already makes you excited before the first bite.\n\nThe portions are generous, the ingredients are fresh, and the overall experience is truly memorable. For anyone who loves Vietnamese noodle soups or wants to try a uniquely rich version of bún riêu, Bề Bề Nội is absolutely worth a visit.\n\nHighly recommended!\nRead more\nWritten November 27, 2025",
